course: dictionary
lesson: 11868
title: Words that come back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can be a thing or an action. You can tell which one from the words around it. «The hunter threw his boomerang, and it curved through the air and flew back to his hand.» Here a boomerang is a thing, a curved piece of wood.
explain: Boomerang can also be a verb, an action. «Her mean plan boomeranged on her when everyone found out.» Her plan did not work on the person she wanted to hurt. It came back and hurt her instead. Ask yourself: is it a thing, or something someone does?
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. If «it came back and hurt her» fits the sentence, you have found the right meaning. If a word does not fit, check the words next to it for clues.
fact: A boomerang is a curved, flat piece of wood.
fact: «Boomerang» can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action).
fact: The boomerang was first made by Aboriginal Australians, who used it for hunting, sport and ceremonies.
fact: «Boomeranged» means had the opposite effect from what was meant, often hurting the person who did it.
fact: Not every boomerang comes back. The ones that do come back are thrown in a special way.
exercise: «The boomerang curved through the air and flew back to the thrower.» What is a boomerang? | A type of rope used for climbing | A long stick used for walking | *A curved, flat piece of wood that can come back when thrown | A small bird that sings at dawn
exercise: «Her mean plan boomeranged on her.» What does boomeranged mean here? | It was carried away by the wind | It made her very happy | *It had the opposite effect and hurt her | It flew back to her hand
exercise: The boomerang was first made by which people? | Ancient Egyptians | Vikings in Norway | *Aboriginal Australians | Romans in Italy
test: «He threw the boomerang, and it came back.» Is boomerang a thing or an action here? | Both at once | An action | *A thing | Neither
test: «His rude joke boomeranged on him in the end.» What does boomeranged suggest? | *His joke hurt him instead | His joke was copied by a friend | His joke was forgotten | His joke made everyone laugh
exam: «Some boomerangs come back to the thrower, but a hunting boomerang may fall to the ground.» What does boomerang mean in this sentence? | A long, straight stick | To come back and hurt the person who did it | A kind of bird that flies back home | *A curved, flat piece of wood used as a thrown object
